    int answer=0;for(int x:out)if(x%2==0)answer++;return answer;
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
Build merged

`drawers` contains two lists, each already sorted from smallest to largest. Combine their numbers into one sorted `merged`. Keep all repeated numbers, including copies from both input lists.

Return the answer

Count the even numbers in `merged`. Store the count in `evenCount`. A number is even when it divides by 2 with no remainder. Complete `pairedDrawersEvenKeyCensus` so it returns `evenCount`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `merged` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the combined length of the two lists. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

